  "alert": {
    "item": "lem-hh-cyclotomic-straightening-spanning",
    "finding": "Step 1.3 states “z^csz^dsY=az^{c+d}Y+z^{c+1}sz^d”, with Y=szs. This identity is false as printed. Set r=2, Q=1, u₁=1, u₂=−1, v=w=1, and use the scalar representation X₁=X₂=1, T₁=s=−1 over Q. All stated relations hold, a=0 and z=Y=1. At c=d=0 the displayed identity reads 1=−1. The cited Neaime source, Lemma 6.2 Case 2 (PDF p.33, https://arxiv.org/pdf/1810.12053), treats the corresponding product without that extra s. This is a local proof-expression defect in the published supplier.",
    "severity": "gap-a-reader-closes"
  }
